# value_type_operators.tkr — §9 operator overloading + readonly methods on value-types, exercised end
# to end on the host build. Each row addresses its scenario BY NAME: `main.tks` asserts the scenario's
# announced value with `teko::assert::eq_i64` and prints `scenario <name>: ok`, the line the row below
# demands. The same program runs through the native value-type lowering and the C typedef lowering; a
# divergence in either backend fails its row.

Feature: value_type_operators — operators and readonly methods on prim/enum/flags value-types (§9)

  Scenario: arith_same_type — Cel + Cel via the left-owning __add (ruling 8, leg 1)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario arith_same_type: ok"

  Scenario: right_side_dispatch — raw + Off via the right-owning __add (ruling 8, leg 2)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario right_side_dispatch: ok"

  Scenario: comparison_and_counterpart — __eq and its mandated counterpart __ne (rulings 3/5)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario comparison_and_counterpart: ok"

  Scenario: enum_method — a readonly instance method on an enum value-type (ruling 12)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario enum_method: ok"

  Scenario: indexed_newtype — operator __index over a []i32-backed newtype (ruling 4)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario indexed_newtype: ok"

  Scenario: flags_method — a readonly instance method on a flags value-type (ruling 12)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario flags_method: ok"
